const BEFORE_STORY_UNION_LINES=[
 'I spent two days mistaking revelation for an injury. How very diligent of me. The doctors supplied their little explanations, and I nearly accepted them. A man can be offered the means to reorder the world and still concern himself with whether he has filled in the correct form.',
 'Union Crown understood what the others could not. Peace cannot depend upon everyone agreeing to behave. Give people an endless choice and they will choose another quarrel. Someone must establish an order they cannot dismantle simply because obedience has become inconvenient.',
 'Boki believed this power belonged to her because she wanted something badly enough. Her nephew, her family, her private grief. I sympathise, of course. But sympathy is no reason to let the future of nations rest in the hands of someone who cannot see beyond a single empty chair.',
 'I returned to her with a clearer understanding of our respective positions. She had awakened something she could not govern. I could govern it. There was no need for another performance about destiny, and certainly no need to pretend that we were equals.',
 'She would call me cruel. They always find an unpleasant word for the person who ends the argument. Let her keep the word. I had come for the power, and this time I would not leave Osaka on my hands and knees.'
];
