/* After the killing blow, Josiah confronts what he has done. */
const BEFORE_STORY_UNION_ENDING_LINES=[
 "Boki…? No. No, get up. We were still arguing. You cannot just… please, say something.",
 "I thought taking the power would make everything clear. But you are lying there, and I cannot remember why winning mattered.",
 "Your hand… you were reaching for something. Was it me? Were you asking me to stop?",
 "Tajiri. You kept saying his name, and I spoke over you. God… he has lost his father, and now I have taken the woman who was trying to find him.",
 "I called your grief small. A single empty chair. How did those words come out of my mouth? How could I look at you and say that?",
 "Union Crown? Tell me what to do. Tell me how to bring her back. You had so much to say before—why are you silent now?",
 "No. I cannot blame you for all of it. I heard her. I saw that she was afraid. And I kept pulling the chains.",
 "I want someone to come through that door and find a decent man standing here. But they would find me beside your body, trying to think of an explanation.",
 "I am sorry, Boki. I know you cannot hear me. I know saying it changes nothing. I just… I cannot bear for those cruel words to be the last things I ever said to you.",
 "I will look for Tajiri. I do not know what I could possibly tell him, and I have no right to ask him to forgive me. But I will find him. Please… let me do that much."
];
